The UE shall include the EPS NAS message container in a REGISTRATION REQUEST message during an initial registration procedure **if**:

1. The UE was previously registered in S1 mode before entering state 5GMM-DEREGISTERED;  
2. The UE has received an "interworking without N26 interface not supported" indication from the network;  
3. An EPS security context and a valid 4G-GUTI are available.  

This applies specifically when the UE is performing initial registration after moving from S1 mode to N1 mode in 5GMM-IDLE mode, as per Clause 5.5.1.3.2 and Clause 4.4.6.

If the SpCellConfig contains spCellConfigDedicated and any of the reference signals used for radio link monitoring are reconfigured by it, the UE shall:

- Stop timer T310 for this cell group, if running;  
- Stop timer T312 for this cell group, if running;  
- Reset counters N310 and N311.

One condition under which timer T310 for a cell group would also be stopped according to RLF timer configuration procedures is:  
**Upon SCG deactivation (as specified in Clause 5.3.5.13b), if bfd-and-RLM is not configured to true.**

A UE determines the MBS frequencies of interest (Clause 5.9.4.3) if:  
1. At least one MBS session it is receiving or interested in is ongoing or about to start;  
2. For that session, SIB21 from the PCell includes one or more MBS FSAIs for the frequency;  
3. The UE’s supportedBandCombination includes a band combination supporting simultaneous reception of the set of MBS frequencies of interest (regardless of current serving cells).  

The **MBS Interest Indication** (Clause 5.9.4.5) includes:  
- `mbs-FreqList`: the determined MBS frequencies of interest, sorted by decreasing interest (using ARFCN-ValueNR or absoluteFrequencySSB);  
- `mbs-Priority`: included if the UE prioritizes MBS reception over unicast bearers.  

Thus, the **contents of the MBS Interest Indication are directly derived from the set of MBS frequencies of interest** determined in Clause 5.9.4.3. The indication is sent when this set is non-empty or has changed, or when MBS reception priority has changed.
